==English==
{{wikipedia|phlogiston theory}}

===Etymology===
Coined by [[w:Georg Ernst Stahl|Stahl]] in 1702, from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|lang=grc|φλογιστόν}}, neuter of {{term|lang=grc|φλογιστός}} ‘inflammable’, from {{term|lang=grc|φλογίζειν}} ‘to set fire to’, from {{term|lang=grc|φλόξ}} ‘flame’. {{attention|grc}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/flə(ʊ)ˈdʒɪstɒn/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{context|chemistry|historical}} The [[hypothetical]] [[fiery]] [[principle]] formerly assumed to be a necessary [[constituent]] of [[combustible]] bodies and to be given up by them in [[burning]].

====Related terms====
* [[dephlogisticated air]]

